# Repair plan for /playwright/playwright:home.spec.ts::home.spec.ts_>_home_page_>_shows_the_store_name_as_its_heading

## Diagnosis

The failing assertion reads the rendered `h1` of the home page:

```
tests/integration/home.spec.ts:9
expect(await page.locator('h1').textContent()).toBe('Corner Shop');
```

Playwright boots the service itself (`webServer.command: 'node ../services/web/server.js'` in `tests/playwright.config.ts`), so the page under test is the exact HTML that `services/web/server.js` serves. That file holds one hard-coded HTML document and its top-level heading currently reads `Welcome`:

```
services/web/server.js:10
    <h1>Welcome</h1>
```

`textContent()` on the single `h1` therefore returns `"Welcome"`, while the spec expects the store's name, `"Corner Shop"` — exactly the `Expected "Corner Shop" / Received "Welcome"` diff in the report. The defect is in production source; the test is correct and must not be touched.

The `<title>Corner Shop</title>` already in the same document (line 8) confirms the intended store name, so there is no ambiguity about the expected string: it is `Corner Shop`, spelled and cased that way.

